From c955134ca99c87ed8bcf3f7fada5a8f4f0a5129a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:52:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: no restart offered under playback; a notice
 for a busy output

Two things that a change of the Monitor setting told the user did not hold:

- under playback, a monitor of the same graphics card was refused ("Stop
  playback to change the monitor."), but one of another card asked whether to
  start Kodi again now, and a yes ended what played. Both are refused the same
  way under playback (a video or music) now; with nothing playing, the question
  is asked as before;
- the notice to stop playback was also shown when nothing played and the
  output still finished a change of its own (OutputMoveBlocked(): the end of
  the HDR signalling or of native Dolby Vision after a video, a change of mode
  that waits, an output that a flip which did not come turned off). That case
  has a notice of its own (#39857): "The output is still finishing a change.
  Wait a moment and try again."
---
